# SHARED BY BOTH VERCEL PROJECTS. Vercel reads this file from the repository
# root for every project built from this repo, whatever its Root Directory --
# so an entry here that suits collider-api can delete the app collider needs.
# `web/` was listed here while the API was the only thing deployed from this
# repo; once collider was git-connected it stripped the Next.js app before the
# build could find it, and the deploy failed with "No Next.js version
# detected". Keep exclusions here to paths neither project builds from.
#
# The API function stays small regardless: vercel.json whitelists its bundle
# with includeFiles, so this file governs the upload, not the function.
# data/raw alone is 230 MB of ROOT files and never leaves this machine.
web/.next/
tests/
scripts/
notebooks/
docs/
assets/
data/raw/
data/interim/
.venv/
.github/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
collider.egg-info/
uv.lock
Dockerfile
